nvk-tex-uhandle-safe: with NAK_TEX_UHANDLE=1 a texture whose handle left its uniform register compiles (3.0.10).
NullMoth's own change (not an upstream Mesa commit).

NAK_TEX_UHANDLE=1 (off by default, SM100 and later) keeps the handle of a TEX in a uniform register, and the encoder
asserts that it is one. Two passes could hand that source a warp register instead, and the compile then panicked: NVK
answered VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN for the pipeline, and the process aborted under NAK_DEBUG=panic.
The first is opt_uniform_instrs: it lowers a uniform instruction that cannot be encoded as one, or that reads two
values that are not uniform, and gives its uses the warp value. A handle loaded by an LDC with a register offset (an
array of samplers indexed by a uniform value) or by a global LD (a descriptor past the part of its set mapped as a
constant buffer) is such a use; those two are the loads that were reproduced. The second is spill_values: when more
uniform values are live than there are uniform registers, it gives every use in a non-uniform block the GPR copy of a
spilled one.
A texture in either state now goes back to the layout from_nir already builds for a handle that is not uniform (the
handle first in the second source, the split of the coordinates undone): in OpTex's legalize for the first case, and
in assign_regs after the uniform registers were spilled for the second, where a value that ends up twice among the
texture's vector sources gets a copy, as legalize gives one. The encoder and its assertion are unchanged.

With NAK_TEX_UHANDLE unset the handle is always Zero: demote_handle returns before it writes anything, and the loop in
assign_regs skips every block. tools/test_nak_tex_uhandle_safe.py reads this patch for those properties.

diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/assign_regs.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/assign_regs.rs
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/assign_regs.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/assign_regs.rs
@@ -1444,6 +1444,49 @@
             }
         }
 
+        // nvk-tex-uhandle-safe: in a non-uniform block spill_values hands every use of a spilled UGPR its GPR copy
+        // ("non-uniform instructions can always accept a wave register"), which the uniform handle of TEX cannot
+        // take. Such a texture goes back to the GPR-handle layout. Undoing its .SCR split can leave one value twice
+        // in a vector (vec2(c, c)), which legalize copies apart and RA cannot place, so a value that is twice among
+        // the vector sources gets a copy, as in legalize (sources of one component are left alone). A block with no
+        // uniform handle, which is every block unless NAK_TEX_UHANDLE=1, is not touched.
+        let mut demoted = false;
+        for b in f.blocks.iter_mut() {
+            if !b.instrs.iter().any(|i| matches!(&i.op, Op::Tex(tex) if !tex.handle.is_zero())) {
+                continue;
+            }
+            let mut instrs = Vec::with_capacity(b.instrs.len() + 1);
+            for mut instr in b.instrs.drain(..) {
+                if let Op::Tex(tex) = &mut instr.op {
+                    if tex.demote_handle() {
+                        demoted = true;
+                        let mut seen: FxHashSet<SSAValue> = Default::default();
+                        for src in tex.srcs.iter_mut() {
+                            if let SrcRef::SSA(vec) = &mut src.src_ref {
+                                if vec.comps() == 1 {
+                                    continue;
+                                }
+                                for c in &mut vec[..] {
+                                    if !seen.insert(*c) {
+                                        let copy = f.ssa_alloc.alloc(c.file());
+                                        instrs.push(Instr::new(OpCopy { dst: copy.into(), src: (*c).into() }));
+                                        *c = copy;
+                                    }
+                                }
+                            }
+                        }
+                    }
+                }
+                instrs.push(instr);
+            }
+            b.instrs = instrs;
+        }
+        if demoted {
+            // the copies are new values and the handle moved between sources
+            live = SimpleLiveness::for_function(f);
+            max_live = live.calc_max_live(f);
+        }
+
         // An instruction can have at most 4 vector sources/destinations.  In
         // order to ensure we always succeed at allocation, regardless of
         // arbitrary choices, we need at least 16 GPRs.
diff --git a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm70_encode.rs b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm70_encode.rs
--- a/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm70_encode.rs
+++ b/src/nouveau/compiler/nak/sm70_encode.rs
@@ -2881,8 +2881,40 @@
     }
 }
 
+impl OpTex {
+    /// nvk-tex-uhandle-safe: TEX takes its uniform handle from a UGPR only (set_ureg asserts the file). When a pass
+    /// has turned the handle into a warp value, the texture goes back to the layout from_nir builds for a handle
+    /// that is not uniform: the handle first in srcs[1], and the .SCR split of the coordinates undone. Before
+    /// register allocation only. Returns false, having changed nothing, for a Zero handle (every texture unless
+    /// NAK_TEX_UHANDLE=1) and for a handle still in a UGPR.
+    pub fn demote_handle(&mut self) -> bool {
+        let h = match &self.handle.src_ref {
+            SrcRef::SSA(h) if h.file() != RegFile::UGPR => h.clone(),
+            _ => return false,
+        };
+        let mut c0: Vec<SSAValue> = Vec::new();
+        let mut c1: Vec<SSAValue> = Vec::new();
+        if let SrcRef::SSA(v) = &self.srcs[0].src_ref { c0.extend(v.iter().copied()); }
+        if let SrcRef::SSA(v) = &self.srcs[1].src_ref { c1.extend(v.iter().copied()); }
+        if self.scalar {
+            c0.extend(c1.drain(..));
+            self.scalar = false;
+        }
+        let mut n1: Vec<SSAValue> = h.iter().copied().collect();
+        n1.extend(c1);
+        self.srcs[0] = SSARef::try_from(&c0[..]).unwrap().into();
+        self.srcs[1] = SSARef::try_from(&n1[..]).unwrap().into();
+        self.handle = SrcRef::Zero.into();
+        true
+    }
+}
+
 impl SM70Op for OpTex {
     fn legalize(&mut self, b: &mut LegalizeBuilder) {
+        // nvk-tex-uhandle-safe: opt_uniform_instrs hands a use the warp value of a uniform instruction it lowered
+        // (a handle loaded by an LDC with a register offset, or by a global LD); such a handle returns to srcs here,
+        // before legalize_tex_instr and the pass after it that keeps a vector's components distinct
+        self.demote_handle();
         legalize_tex_instr(self, b);
     }
 
